      ******************************************************************
      * DCLGEN TABLE(CHK_RETURN_TXN)                                   *
      *        LIBRARY(PROD.CHK.DCLGEN(CHKRTNDG))                      *
      *        LANGUAGE(COBOL)                                         *
      *        QUOTE                                                   *
      ******************************************************************
           EXEC SQL DECLARE CHK_RETURN_TXN TABLE
           ( CHECK_NO                       CHAR(10) NOT NULL,
             ACCT_NO                        CHAR(12) NOT NULL,
             CHECK_AMT                      DECIMAL(13, 2) NOT NULL,
             FEE_AMT                        DECIMAL(9, 2) NOT NULL,
             RETURN_DATE                    DATE NOT NULL,
             REASON_CODE                    CHAR(2) NOT NULL,
             POST_FLAG                      CHAR(1) NOT NULL
           ) END-EXEC.
      ******************************************************************
      * COBOL DECLARATION FOR TABLE CHK_RETURN_TXN                     *
      ******************************************************************
       01  DCLCHK-RETURN-TXN.
           10 CHECK-NO             PIC X(10).
           10 ACCT-NO              PIC X(12).
           10 CHECK-AMT            PIC S9(11)V9(2) USAGE COMP-3.
           10 FEE-AMT              PIC S9(7)V9(2) USAGE COMP-3.
           10 RETURN-DATE          PIC X(10).
           10 REASON-CODE          PIC X(2).
           10 POST-FLAG            PIC X(1).
      ******************************************************************
      * THE NUMBER OF COLUMNS DESCRIBED BY THIS DECLARATION IS 7       *
      ******************************************************************
